<p>France has ordered its nuclear-powered aircraft carrier, the Charles de Gaulle, to redeploy to the Mediterranean as the war in the Middle East widens, including conflict involving Iran. President Emmanuel Macron said the move is meant to help protect allied assets. The carrier is sailing with an escort of frigates and its air wing. In a televised address, Macron called France’s posture “strictly defensive,” while also criticizing US and Israeli military operations as being conducted “outside international law,” according to reporting on his remarks. The deployment underscores European concern that the conflict could spread and bring security risks closer to Europe, even as French officials cast the move as protective rather than escalatory.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/bn29IoWnrpN4y7azTHF0vgszcboKCyegjwdoHmKUuMfy9AC4HKAtqhC-Io_h7LlCRyHiCsOB6zYzEc8WH2rG6xhy6VQ6jKyw1T1z0Ttx6guCwu-K_x-3xw-94jXygwkV-c6FeFFmWBPyB1S-JzG72ZRwCjqM3QN7hcCaAZNo6Q1Q-J_z' alt='The French aircraft carrier Charles-de-Gaulle off the coast of Toulon, in the Mediterranean, June 5, 2021.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>More air cover: Macron said France had deployed Rafale fighter jets, air-defence systems and airborne radar assets to the region in the preceding hours.</li><li>Leaving the Baltic: Macron ordered the Charles de Gaulle to move from the Baltic Sea to the Mediterranean as the Middle East war intensifies.</li><li>A day after his warning: Macron announced the move in a televised address, one day after saying the conflict could spill over Europe’s borders.</li><li>Where it’s headed: Le Monde said the carrier is bound for the eastern Mediterranean.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Emmanuel Macron (French presidency): Macron said he ordered the Charles de Gaulle, its air assets and an escort of frigates to set course for the Mediterranean. He announced the move a day after warning the conflict could spill over Europe’s borders. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/france-deploys-aircraft-carrier-mediterranean-over-iran-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Le Monde on Macron’s address: Le Monde described a solemn speech announcing several measures, including sending the carrier to the eastern Mediterranean, and reported that Macron acknowledged the risk of a wider regional conflict. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/04/france-enters-iran-conflict-in-a-strictly-defensive-posture_6751076_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Macron on US-Israel operations: Macron said the United States and Israel chose to launch military operations that he said were conducted outside international law, which France “cannot approve.” (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/macron-orders-frances-nuclear-powered-aircraft-carrier-to-mediterranean/article70701126.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/macron-orders-frances-nuclear-powered-aircraft-carrier-mediterranean-130726610'>Macron orders France&#x27;s nuclear-powered aircraft carrier to the Mediterranean</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/04/france-enters-iran-conflict-in-a-strictly-defensive-posture_6751076_4.html'>France enters Iran conflict in a &#x27;strictly defensive&#x27; posture</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/macron-orders-frances-nuclear-powered-aircraft-carrier-to-move-from-baltic-sea-to-mediterranean'>Macron orders France&#x27;s nuclear-powered aircraft carrier to move from Baltic Sea to Mediterranean</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3345329/iran-war-macron-orders-frances-nuclear-powered-aircraft-carrier-mediterranean'>Iran war: Macron orders France’s nuclear-powered aircraft carrier to the Mediterranean</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/macron-orders-frances-nuclear-powered-aircraft-carrier-